    </p>

    <h2>4. Workspaces, roles, and ownership</h2>
    <p>
        ProcureCore organises content in studio workspaces. Roles include owner, admin, member, and read-only viewer. Workspace owners control ownership and membership decisions; admins and members have the operational permissions assigned to their roles.
    </p>
    <p>
        Content added to a shared workspace forms part of that studio’s business record and is available to authorised members. A user leaving or transferring ownership may need to decide what happens to affected workspaces. Shared records can remain for the studio after an individual leaves.
    </p>
    <p>
        Studios are responsible for the people they invite, for assigning appropriate roles, and for ensuring their team enters and uses information lawfully.
    </p>

